20</volume><fpage>60</fpage><lpage>63</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b7-ehp0115-000889"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahsan</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Cancer burden from arsenic in drinking water in Bangladesh</article-title><source>Am J Public Health</source><volume>94</volume><fpage>741</fpage><lpage>744</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15117692</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8-ehp0115-000889"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Chowdhury</surname><given-names>UK</given-names></name><name><surname>Biswas</surname><given-names>BK</given-names></name><name><surname>Chowdhury</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>Samanta</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Mandal</surname><given-names>BK</given-names></name><name><surname>Basu</surname><given-names>GC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Groundwater arsenic contamination in Bangladesh and West Bengal, India</article-title><source>Environ Health Perspect</source><volume>108</volume><fpage>393</fpage><lpage>397</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10811564</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ehp0115-000889"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Duxbury</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mayer</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Lauren</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><name><surname>Hassan</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Food chain aspects of arsenic contamination in Bangladesh: effects on quality and productivity of rice</article-title><source>J Environ Sci Health A Tox Hazard Subst Environ Eng</source><volume>38</volume><fpage>61</fpage><lpage>69</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12635819</pub-id></citatio